\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Father of all! Whose powerful voice
\par Called forth this universal frame; 
\par Whose mercies over all rejoice,
\par Through endless ages still the same:
\par   \tab 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thou by Thy word upholdest all;
\par Thy bounteous love to all is showed,
\par Thou hear'st Thy every creature's call, 
\par And fillest every mouth with good.
\par  
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Giver and Lord of life, whose power 
\par And guardian care for all are free,
\par To Thee, in fierce temptation's hour,
\par From sin and Satan let us flee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4Thine, Lord, we are, and ours Thou art;
\par In us be all Thy goodness showed.
\par Renew, enlarge and fill our heart 
\par With peace, and joy, and heaven, and God. 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Father, 'tis Thine each day to yield
\par Thy children's want a fresh supply;
\par Thou cloth'st the lilies of the field,
\par And hearest the young ravens cry. 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. On Thee we cast our care; we live 
\par Through Thee, who know'st our every need:   \tab 
\par O feed us with Thy grac, and give 
\par Our souls this day the living bread. 
\par                                          Amen.
\par \lang1033\f1 
\par \cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

